An equilateral triangle with side length 2 is rotated about one vertex by an angle of $\theta,$ where $0^\circ < \theta < 60^\circ$ and $\sin \theta = \frac{2}{3}.$  Find the area of the shaded region that is common to both triangles.

[asy]
unitsize(3 cm);

pair A, B, C, Bp, Cp, P;

A = (0,0);
B = (0,-1);
C = (0.5,1);
Bp = rotate(aSin(2/3))*(B);
Cp = rotate(aSin(2/3))*(C);
P = extension(C,B,Bp,Cp);

fill(A--Bp--P--C--cycle,gray(0.7));
draw(A--B---C--cycle);
draw(A--Bp--Cp--cycle);

label("$\theta$", A + (-0.25,0.1));
[/asy]

In the diagram below, four congruent right triangles are placed inside a large rectangle. If the area of each right triangle is 54 square centimeters, what is the area of the rectangle?

[asy]
unitsize(1cm);
defaultpen(linewidth(0.7pt));

draw((0,0)--(3,0)--(3,3)--(0,3)--cycle);
draw((0,3)--(3,0));
draw((0,0)--(1,2));
draw((3,0)--(2,1));
draw((3,3)--(1,2));
draw((0,3)--(2,1));
[/asy]

Consider the function $g(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
x^2 & \text{ if }x\text{ is an integer}, \\
\frac{1}{x} & \text{ if }x\text{ is a rational number, not an integer}, \\
x+1 & \text{ if }x\text{ is irrational}.
\end{array}
\right.$

Let $x_0$ be a number such that $g^{n}(x_0) = x_0$ for some positive integer $n$. Determine the maximum value of $n$.

In the diagram shown, $\overrightarrow{OA}\perp\overrightarrow{OC}$ and $\overrightarrow{OB}\perp\overrightarrow{OD}$. If $\angle{AOD}$ is 3.5 times $\angle{BOC}$, what is $\angle{AOD}$? [asy]
unitsize(1.5cm);
defaultpen(linewidth(.7pt)+fontsize(10pt));
dotfactor=4;

pair O=(0,0), A=dir(0), B=dir(50), C=dir(90), D=dir(140);
pair[] dots={O,A,B,C,D};

dot(dots);
draw(O--1.2*D,EndArrow(4));
draw(O--1.2*B,EndArrow(4));
draw(O--1.2*C,EndArrow(4));
draw(O--1.2*A,EndArrow(4));

label("$D$",D,SW);
label("$C$",C,W);
label("$B$",B,E);
label("$A$",A,N);
label("$O$",O,S);
[/asy]

Let  \[ f(x) =
\begin{cases}
-x^2 & \text{if } x \geq 0,\\
x+8& \text{if } x <0.
\end{cases}
\]Compute $f(f(f(f(f(1))))).$

A function $g(x)$ is defined as follows:
\[ g(x) =
\begin{cases}
-x & \text{if } x \geq 0,\\
-x^2& \text{if } x <0.
\end{cases}
\]Find the value of $x$ such that $g(g(g(g(x)))) = -7$.

In the figure shown, all 25 of the circles are congruent and are tangent to their adjacent circles and to the sides of the square.  The length of a side of the square is 48.  Find the area of the shaded region.

[asy]
unitsize(0.4 cm);

draw((0,0)--(6,0)--(6,6)--(0,6)--cycle);

for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {
draw((i+0.5,0)--(i+0.5,0.5));
draw((i+0.5,5.5)--(i+0.5,6));
draw((0,i+0.5)--(0.5,i+0.5));
draw((5.5,i+0.5)--(6,i+0.5));
}

for (int i = 0; i < 3; ++i) {
for (int j = 0; j < 3; ++j) {
draw(Circle((i+1,j+1),1));
}
}
[/asy]
